{%- comment -%}
  CONTEXTUAL FAQs ON A PRODUCT PAGE.

  Slice 12. README: "Allow reusable contextual FAQs on product pages and
  product-specific entries when truly needed."

  Reads the product metafield `carat.faq_entries` — a LIST OF METAOBJECT
  REFERENCES pointing at `faq_entry` entries. Namespace `carat` matches every
  other CaratForUs product metafield (`carat.bank_payment_price_minor_units`,
  `carat.luxury_steal`).

  ============================================================================
  REUSABLE BY REFERENCE, WHICH IS THE WHOLE POINT
  ============================================================================
  The metafield holds REFERENCES, not copies. One "How do I find my ring
  size?" entry can be attached to fifty products, and editing it once updates
  all fifty. The alternative — per-product FAQ text — is fifty copies that
  drift, which is the same mistake the policy pages exist to avoid.

  So this snippet contains no FAQ content and no fallback content. A product
  with nothing attached renders nothing.

  RENDERS THROUGH `faq-list`, the same renderer the FAQ page uses, so an
  answer cannot look different in the two places it appears.

  ACCEPTS:
    product  the product object (required)
    heading  optional heading (default below)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign faq_refs = product.metafields.carat.faq_entries.value
  assign faq_heading = heading | default: 'Questions about this piece'
-%}

{%- if faq_refs != blank and faq_refs.size > 0 -%}
  {%- render 'faq-list',
    entries: faq_refs,
    heading: faq_heading,
    heading_size: 'h3',
    show_category: false
  -%}
{%- endif -%}
